{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HyMpdfY6FGdVbeZBFZuz3H","type":"tool_result","content":"<persisted-output>\nOutput too large (52.4KB). Full output saved to: /home/ubuntu/.claude-account-1/projects/-home-ubuntu--agent-ml-research-idea-gen-0509-9-projects-event-gated-adaptive-horizon/897ba80d-7ac0-4ab3-8af6-91e374677a7e/tool-results/toolu_01HyMpdfY6FGdVbeZBFZuz3H.txt\n\nPreview (first 2KB):\n{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_9/projects/event-gated-adaptive-horizon/literature_map.yaml\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"# Literature Map — event-gated-adaptive-horizon\\\\n# Last updated: 2026-05-14\\\\n# Total: 72 papers (64 existing + 8 incremental scan 2026-05-14)\\\\n\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# EXISTING CITATIONS (already in paper.tex)\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: sutton1999options\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Between MDPs and Semi-MDPs: A Framework for Temporal Abstraction in Reinforcement Learning\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Sutton R.S., Precup D., Singh S.]\\\\n  year: 1999\\\\n  venue: \\\\\\\"Artificial Intelligence 112(1-2):181-211\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: background\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Foundational options framework for temporal abstraction in RL; our work investigates why temporal abstraction fails in world-model RL\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 5\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: hafner2020dreamerv1\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Dream to Control: Learning Behaviors by Latent Imagination\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Hafner D., Lillicrap T., Ba J., Norouzi M.]\\\\n  year: 2020\\\\n  venue: ICLR\\\\n  category: background\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"DreamerV1 — base architecture family; our experiments build on the RSSM and imagination-based training paradigm\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 5\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: hafner2023dreamerv3\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Mastering Diverse Domains through Worl